182 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 471 0 R
/E (Redundant Iteration Passes \(Local Stability\): The algorithm re-traverses all nodes in every iteration of Phase 1. However, once a pair of communities reach a "local stable structure" \(i.e., no modularity gain is possible between them\), the calculation is repeated needlessly. This means repeated, unnecessary calculations of the Modularity Gain \(      \) for stable pairs. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
183 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 472 0 R
/E (Slow Convergence on Sparse Structures: Many real-world networks contain sparse leaf nodes and local tree structures \(long chains\). Including these structurally unambiguous nodes in the main iteration wastes time and slows the convergence of the entire graph.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
184 0 obj
<<
